     E*
     E* RPG/400 extension and line counter specifications, and the
     E* compile-time records that follow the last specification.
     E*
     E* Member: RPGEXT   Compilable: no (declarations only, no cycle)
     E* Source: RPG/400 Reference SC09-1817, chapters 6, 7, 13 and 15
     E*         (Tables 19 and 20).
     E* Retrieved: 2026-07-26
     E*
     E* 11-18 from file  19-26 to file  27-32 array or table name
     E* 33-35 entries per record  36-39 entries per array or table
     E* 40-42 length of entry  43 format  44 decimals  45 sequence
     E* 46-51 alternating name  52-54 length  55 format  56 decimals
     E* 57 sequence  58-74 and 75-80 comments
     E*  1         2         3         4         5         6         7         8
     E*8901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890
     E*
     E* Compile-time array: no from file, entries per record given.
     E                    ARC    12  12  3               Part codes
     E                    MTH     1  12 10               Month names
     E*
     E* Prerun-time array: the from file loads it before the first cycle.
     E    TAXFILE         TAXRAT     50  5P4
     E    RATEFILERATEOUT RATE      100  7 2
     E*
     E* Run-time array: neither file named, loaded by calculations.
     E                    TOTALS     24  9 2
     E                    FLAGS      99  1
     E*
     E* Binary, packed and signed entries, ascending and descending.
     E                    BINARR     10  4B0A
     E                    PCKARR     10  8P2D
     E                    LFTARR     10  6L0A
     E                    RGTARR     10  6R0D
     E*
     E* Alternating format: two tables share one set of records.
     E                    TABPRT  1 250  5  ATABDSC 30  APart and description
     E    CODEFILE        TABCDE    100  3  ATABAMT  9P2
     E*
     E* A page and line number in 1-5 does not disturb the columns,
     E* including the comment area, which starts at 58 on an E spec.
03010E                    SEQARR     10  3               numbered E spec
     L*
     L* Line counter: 15-17 lines per page, 18-19 FL,
     L* 20-22 overflow line, 23-24 OL.
     LQSYSPRT  66FL 60OL                                                  66/60
     LRPTFILE 112FL106OL
     LLABELS    6FL  5OL
03020LSEQPRT   66FL 60OL                                                  seq
      *
      * Records after the last specification are loaded at compile
      * time. Each group is introduced by ** in positions 1-3.
      * File translation records come first, then the alternate
      * collating sequence, then array and table data.
**    File translation table
*FILES  C1F1C2F2
ORDHDR  4A5B4B5C
**    Alternate collating sequence
ALTSEQ  C1C2C2C3
**    Compile-time array ARC, twelve entries per record
48K16343J640 44H12648A47349K3465 0B125
**    Compile-time array MTH, one entry per record
JANUARY
FEBRUARY
MARCH
APRIL
MAY
JUNE
JULY
AUGUST
SEPTEMBER
OCTOBER
NOVEMBER
DECEMBER
